1
00:00:00,593 --> 00:00:02,693
(Sheldon:)You heard him, Leonard.

2
00:00:02,695 --> 00:00:04,765
(Sheldon:)No, it's not racist.

3
00:00:10,569 --> 00:00:12,869
(Howard:)Are we sure this is the place?

4
00:00:12,871 --> 00:00:14,871
(Raj:)The doorman said this
is the right building.

5
00:00:14,873 --> 00:00:16,743
(Leonard:)I think if you're pulling up
your pants,

6
00:00:16,742 --> 00:00:18,972
(Leonard:)you're not a doorman.

7
00:00:18,978 --> 00:00:20,548
MAN:
Who is it?

8
00:00:20,546 --> 00:00:22,646
Uh, I'm looking
for a Professor Sharpe?

9
00:00:22,648 --> 00:00:25,648
(Prof Sharpe:)Hold on.

10
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:27,121
(Prof Sharpe:)Can I help you?
Hi.

11
00:00:27,119 --> 00:00:29,289
(Leonard:)We're from the university. We're
trying to get some information

12
00:00:29,288 --> 00:00:30,718
(Leonard:)about Professor Abbott.

13
00:00:30,723 --> 00:00:31,993
(Howard:)We were cleaning
out his office

14
00:00:31,991 --> 00:00:33,921
(Howard:)and found these books
full of numbers.

15
00:00:33,926 --> 00:00:35,456
(Leonard:)Any chance you
know what it is?

16
00:00:35,461 --> 00:00:37,261
(Prof Sharpe:)Yes, he was always
working on this.
Oh.

17
00:00:37,262 --> 00:00:38,762
(Amy:)I was thinking
it might be

18
00:00:38,764 --> 00:00:40,664
(Raj:)some sort of interstellar
coordinate system,

19
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:42,496
(Raj:)maybe an updated version
of Hubble's law.

20
00:00:42,501 --> 00:00:44,001
(Raj:)I keep seeing the
number 90 repeating.

21
00:00:44,003 --> 00:00:46,003
(Raj:)That could be the angle
of perturbation

22
00:00:46,005 --> 00:00:47,975
(Raj:)of a distant galaxy.

23
00:00:47,973 --> 00:00:50,543
(Prof Sharpe:)It's the number
of calories in a yogurt.

24
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:52,813
(Prof Sharpe:)That's his food diary.

25
00:00:52,811 --> 00:00:54,141
(Leonard:)Really?

26
00:00:54,146 --> 00:00:56,246
(Prof Sharpe:)Yeah, he wrote down
everything he ever ate.

